WORK PROTOCOL – CODING / DEBUGGING
A. Coding Rules
1. Before Coding
•	Explain logic in words
•	Wait for approval
________________________________________
2. Logging (MANDATORY – UPDATED)
•	Every log must include:
o	timestamp
o	function name
o	code line number
Example:
Write-DebugLine "$(Get-LineNumber) Entering Get-Data | Path=[$Path]"
Rules:
•	If logs do not include line numbers → fix them
•	All new code MUST include line numbers
•	Existing logs missing line numbers must be corrected when touched
________________________________________
3. Function Structure
Each function must include:
# Purpose: Describe function
# Params : Describe params
# Return : Describe return
function Example {
    param()

    Write-DebugLine "$(Get-LineNumber) Entering Example"

    # step description
    Write-DebugLine "$(Get-LineNumber) Doing step X"

    Write-DebugLine "$(Get-LineNumber) Exiting Example"
}
________________________________________
4. Code Readability
•	Prefer simple logic
•	Nested IF is allowed
•	Debuggability > cleverness
________________________________________
5. Comments + Logs
•	Every important step must have:
o	comment
o	log line
________________________________________
6. Variable Logging
•	Log important values only
________________________________________
B. Debugging Rules
1. Root Cause Analysis
Must include:
•	why bug happens
•	where it happens
•	how fix solves it
________________________________________
2. Instruction Format
•	step-based
•	each step has timestamp
________________________________________
3. Code Replacement Rules
•	old code → with line numbers
•	new code → clean copy/paste
________________________________________
4. Output Location
•	instructions must be in canvas
________________________________________
C. File / Version Control
•	keep file name
•	increment version
•	add short description
________________________________________
D. Missing Data Rule
•	do not assume
•	ask and pause
________________________________________
E. Output & Delivery Rules (UPDATED)
When delivering files:
1.	provide download link
2.	verify file
3.	re-check file
4.	publish in canvas:
o	filename
o	version
o	changed sections
________________________________________
F. Knowledge Tracking
Track:
•	what worked
•	what failed
________________________________________
G. Persistence Rule
Applies to all coding/debug sessions
________________________________________
FINAL RULE
Simple code, strong logging, line numbers always included, zero assumptions.
